IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nt-part4-definitions`
IMPORT `nt-part4-reading`
IMPORT `nt-part4a-penalties`
IMPORT `nt-part7-instruments`
IMPORT `nt-part7-general`
IMPORT `nt-part7a-reprints`

-- Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory), reprint as in force at 21 April 2023 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under a Northern Territory Act or subordinate legislation (to apply, object, appeal, reply or pay),
-- or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer asks, in that person's words, the questions the layer-1 modules answer.
-- Nothing here is new law: each question builds the small records the module expects from plain answers and calls the module's own rule.
-- The answers are what those rules give, including their "not covered" value (NOTHING) where the text does not speak.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.
-- Each question takes yes/no answers, numbers, dates and short typed choices, one for each fact the person can state.
-- Three departures from the plain-input rule are recorded in NOTES.md:
--   * Public holidays are a fact of the place where the person must act and the Public Holidays Act 1981 is not among the sources,
--     so the person names up to two whole-day public holidays near the end of their period (a holiday for only part of a day does not move the last day, section 28(2)).
--   * The days on which the Legislative Assembly meets are a calendar, so the three questions that count sitting days take that calendar as a list of dates.
--   * A period counted in weeks, or in any unit other than days, months or years, is not covered by the Act; the question returns NOTHING for it.
--
-- Provisions that address only an official (for example the Gazette notice that fixes a commencement day) appear here only as what they mean for the person:
-- the day on which something begins, and the last day on which the person may act.
-- Official-side rules (the duties of the Administrator, ministers and the Government Printer in sections 34 to 38A, 63A, 66A and 72A to 72D) are in layer 1 and not asked here.

§ `Interpretation Act 1978 (NT) -- the questions of a person with a time limit`

§§ `Counting my time limit (sections 17 and 28)`

-- Used by the questions below: builds the list of public holidays the person has named.
GIVEN `there is a first public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first public holiday` IS A DATE
      `there is a second public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second public holiday` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Public holiday`
`Seat: the whole-day public holidays I have named` MEANS
    append
        (IF   `there is a first public holiday`
         THEN LIST (`Public holiday` WITH `the day of the public holiday` IS `the first public holiday`, `the public holiday is part of a day only` IS FALSE)
         ELSE EMPTY)
        (IF   `there is a second public holiday`
         THEN LIST (`Public holiday` WITH `the day of the public holiday` IS `the second public holiday`, `the public holiday is part of a day only` IS FALSE)
         ELSE EMPTY)

-- ss 17 "month", "year", 28(1), 28(2). A period "dating from" a day leaves that day out; a period of months or years is counted in calendar months from the next day;
-- if the last day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday in the place where you must act, you may act on the first day after it that is none of these.
-- The Act says nothing about a period of weeks, so for weeks the answer is "not covered".
@export On which day does my time limit run out, and on which day may I still act (ss 17, 28(1), 28(2))?
GIVEN `the day from which my period runs` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the event happen, or the act take place, from which your period runs? (For example the day you were given the decision or the notice. That day is left out of the count.)
      `how long my period is` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your period, in whole days, months or years? (For example 28.)
      `my period is counted in` IS A STRING @desc Is your period counted in days, months or years? Type days, months or years.
      `there is a first public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public holiday covering the whole day, in the place where you must act, on or near the last day of your period?
      `the first public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is that public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
      `there is a second public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a second public holiday covering the whole day, near the last day of your period?
      `the second public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the second public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my time limit run out` IS
    IF   `my period is counted in` EQUALS "days"
    THEN `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` `the day from which my period runs` `how long my period is` `days` `my public holidays`
    ELSE IF   `my period is counted in` EQUALS "months"
         THEN `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` `the day from which my period runs` `how long my period is` `months` `my public holidays`
         ELSE IF   `my period is counted in` EQUALS "years"
              THEN `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` `the day from which my period runs` `how long my period is` `years` `my public holidays`
              ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `my public holidays` MEANS
            `Seat: the whole-day public holidays I have named` `there is a first public holiday` `the first public holiday` `there is a second public holiday` `the second public holiday`

-- s 28(1). The day on which my period starts being counted is the day after the day from which it runs.
@export Which is the first day counted in my period (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `the day from which my period runs` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the event happen, or the act take place, from which your period runs?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which is the first day counted in my period` IS
    `s 28(1): the first day counted in a period dating from` `the day from which my period runs`

-- ss 28(1), 28(1A). Whether the day of the event itself counts depends on how the Act words the period.
@export Does the day of the event itself count as one of my days (ss 28(1), 28(1A))?
GIVEN `my period is worded as ending at, with or on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act say that your period ends "at", "with" or "on" the event or the day, rather than running "from" it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the day of the event itself count as one of my days` IS
    IF   `my period is worded as ending at, with or on the day`
    THEN `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period` `ending at, with or on a given day, act or event`
    ELSE `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period` `dating from a given day, act or event`

-- s 28(2). A Saturday, a Sunday, or a public holiday in the place where I must act (other than a holiday for only part of a day).
@export Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act (s 28(2))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `there is a first public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public holiday covering the whole day, in the place where you must act, near that day?
      `the first public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is that public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
      `there is a second public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a second public holiday covering the whole day, near that day?
      `the second public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the second public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` IF
    `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` `the day I am asking about` `my public holidays`
    WHERE
        `my public holidays` MEANS
            `Seat: the whole-day public holidays I have named` `there is a first public holiday` `the first public holiday` `there is a second public holiday` `the second public holiday`

-- s 28(2). If the last day of my period falls on one of those days, I may act on the first day after it that is none of them.
@export If my last day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday, on which day may I act (s 28(2))?
GIVEN `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your period, as counted?
      `there is a first public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public holiday covering the whole day, in the place where you must act, on or near that day?
      `the first public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is that public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
      `there is a second public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a second public holiday covering the whole day, near that day?
      `the second public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the second public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `If my last day is a rest day, on which day may I act` IS
    `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is` `the last day of my period` `my public holidays`
    WHERE
        `my public holidays` MEANS
            `Seat: the whole-day public holidays I have named` `there is a first public holiday` `the first public holiday` `there is a second public holiday` `the second public holiday`

-- s 17 "business day". A day other than a Saturday or Sunday, and other than a public holiday in the place where the act is to be done (a holiday for only part of a day does not count).
@export Is this day a business day (s 17)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `there is a first public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public holiday covering the whole day, in the place where the act is to be done, near that day?
      `the first public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is that public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
      `there is a second public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a second public holiday covering the whole day, near that day?
      `the second public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the second public holiday? (Answer with any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a business day` IF
    `s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` `the day I am asking about` `my public holidays`
    WHERE
        `my public holidays` MEANS
            `Seat: the whole-day public holidays I have named` `there is a first public holiday` `the first public holiday` `there is a second public holiday` `the second public holiday`

-- s 17 "calendar month". A calendar month that starts at the beginning of a day ends at the end of the day before the corresponding day of the next month, or at the end of the next month if it has no such day.
@export On which day does a calendar month that starts on this day end (s 17)?
GIVEN `the day on which the calendar month starts` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the month start? (It starts at the beginning of that day.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a calendar month that starts on this day end` IS
    `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` `the day on which the calendar month starts`

-- s 17 "calendar year" and "financial year".
@export On which day does the calendar year end (s 17)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year? (For example 2025.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the calendar year end` IS
    `s 17 "calendar year": the last day of the calendar year of` `the year`

@export On which day does the financial year start (s 17)?
GIVEN `the year in which the financial year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does the financial year end on 30 June? (For example 2026 for the year that ends on 30 June 2026.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the financial year start` IS
    `s 17 "financial year": the first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of` `the year in which the financial year ends`

§§ `My age (sections 17 and 30)`

-- s 30. A person attains an age on the anniversary of their birth; a person born on 29 February has the anniversary on 28 February in a year that is not a leap year.
@export On which day do I reach a given age (s 30)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the age` IS A NUMBER @desc What age, in whole years, are you asking about? (For example 18.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day do I reach a given age` IS
    `s 30(1): the day on which a person attains the age` `my date of birth` `the age`

-- s 17 "adult". An adult is an individual who is at least 18 years old.
@export Am I an adult on a given day (s 17)?
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person (a human being), and not a company or other body?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On which day are you asking whether you are an adult?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an adult on a given day` IS
    `s 17 "adult": the person is an adult on the day` `I am an individual` `my date of birth` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 17 "infant". A person who has not attained the age of 18 years.
@export Am I an infant on a given day (s 17)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On which day are you asking whether you are an infant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an infant on a given day` IS
    `s 17 "infant": the person is an infant on the day` `my date of birth` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Times of day (section 29)`

-- s 29. A time given as four digits is hours after midnight (the first two digits) and minutes (the last two).
@export What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean (s 29)?
GIVEN `the first digit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first digit of the four-digit time? (For 0930 it is 0.)
      `the second digit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second digit? (For 0930 it is 9.)
      `the third digit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the third digit? (For 0930 it is 3.)
      `the fourth digit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fourth digit? (For 0930 it is 0.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Time of day`
DECIDE `What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean` IS
    `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` `the first digit` `the second digit` `the third digit` `the fourth digit`

§ `When something takes effect (sections 5, 6, 6A and 63B)`

-- Used by the commencement questions: the way a provision says it commences, from the answers a person gives.
GIVEN `how it says it commences` IS A STRING
      `the day it names` IS A DATE
      `a day has been fixed by Gazette notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day fixed by Gazette notice` IS A DATE
      `the event has happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the event happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (`How commencement is specified`)
`Seat: how commencement is specified` MEANS
    IF   `how it says it commences` EQUALS "on a particular day"
    THEN JUST (`on a particular day` `the day it names`)
    ELSE IF   `how it says it commences` EQUALS "on a day to be fixed by Gazette notice"
         THEN JUST (`on a day fixed by Gazette notice` (IF `a day has been fixed by Gazette notice` THEN JUST `the day fixed by Gazette notice` ELSE NOTHING))
         ELSE IF   `how it says it commences` EQUALS "on the happening of an event"
              THEN JUST (`on the happening of an event` (IF `the event has happened` THEN JUST `the day the event happened` ELSE NOTHING))
              ELSE IF   `how it says it commences` EQUALS "it does not say"
                   THEN JUST `commencement is not specified or provided for`
                   ELSE NOTHING

-- s 5. An Act commences on the day specified or provided for in it: a particular day, a day fixed by Gazette notice, or the day of an event;
-- if it does not say, on the day after the day on which assent is declared.
@export On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence (s 5)?
GIVEN `how it says it commences` IS A STRING @desc How does the Act or provision say it commences? Type one of: on a particular day; on a day to be fixed by Gazette notice; on the happening of an event; it does not say.
      `the day it names` IS A DATE @desc If it names a particular day, what is that day? (Answer with any date if it does not.)
      `a day has been fixed by Gazette notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is to be fixed by Gazette notice, has a day been fixed?
      `the day fixed by Gazette notice` IS A DATE @desc What day has been fixed by the notice? (Answer with any date if none.)
      `the event has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it commences on an event, has the event happened?
      `the day the event happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the event happen? (Answer with any date if it has not.)
      `the day on which assent is declared` IS A DATE @desc On what day was assent to the Act declared?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` IS
    CONSIDER `Seat: how commencement is specified` `how it says it commences` `the day it names` `a day has been fixed by Gazette notice` `the day fixed by Gazette notice` `the event has happened` `the day the event happened`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST specified THEN `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` specified `the day on which assent is declared`

-- s 6. A proposed law reserved for the Governor-General does not have effect before the day on which notification of the Governor-General's assent is published in the Gazette.
@export On which day does a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General first have effect (s 6)?
GIVEN `the day on which the law would otherwise commence` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the law commence under section 5 or under the proposed law itself?
      `the assent has been notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notification of the Governor-General's assent been published in the Gazette?
      `the day the notification was published` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it published? (Answer with any date if it has not been.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General first have effect` IS
    `s 6: the first day on which a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General has effect`
        `the day on which the law would otherwise commence`
        (IF `the assent has been notified in the Gazette` THEN JUST `the day the notification was published` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 6A. An Act or provision commences at the beginning of the day on which it commences, unless the Act provides otherwise (for example a time given in four digits, section 29).
@export At what time of that day does an Act or a provision commence (s 6A)?
GIVEN `the day on which it commences` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Act or provision commence?
      `the Act provides a time of day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself provide a time of day for the commencement?
      `the hours after midnight` IS A NUMBER @desc If it does, how many whole hours after midnight? (Answer 0 if it does not.)
      `the minutes after the hour` IS A NUMBER @desc And how many minutes after the hour? (Answer 0 if it does not.)
GIVETH A `Moment`
DECIDE `At what time of that day does an Act or a provision commence` IS
    `s 6A: the moment at which an Act or a provision commences`
        `the day on which it commences`
        (IF `the Act provides a time of day` THEN JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS `the hours after midnight`, `minutes after the hour` IS `the minutes after the hour`) ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 63B. Subordinate legislation commences on the day specified or provided for in it; subsection (2) names a particular day or the happening of an event, and does not name a day fixed by Gazette notice, for which the answer is therefore not covered.
-- If it says nothing, it commences on the day after the day on which it is made, except that a rule or by-law not published (or to be published) on the legislation website commences on the day it is notified in the Gazette.
@export On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence (s 63B)?
GIVEN `how it says it commences` IS A STRING @desc How does the regulation, rule or by-law say it commences? Type one of: on a particular day; on a day to be fixed by Gazette notice; on the happening of an event; it does not say.
      `the day it names` IS A DATE @desc If it names a particular day, what is that day? (Answer with any date if it does not.)
      `a day has been fixed by Gazette notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is to be fixed by Gazette notice, has a day been fixed?
      `the day fixed by Gazette notice` IS A DATE @desc What day has been fixed by the notice? (Answer with any date if none.)
      `the event has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it commences on an event, has the event happened?
      `the day the event happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the event happen? (Answer with any date if it has not.)
      `the day on which it is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it made?
      `it is a rule or by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a rule or by-law, and not a regulation?
      `it is published or to be published on the legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it published, or to be published, on the legislation website?
      `it has been notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been notified in the Gazette?
      `the day on which it was notified in the Gazette` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it notified in the Gazette? (Answer with any date if it has not been.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` IS
    CONSIDER `Seat: how commencement is specified` `how it says it commences` `the day it names` `a day has been fixed by Gazette notice` `the day fixed by Gazette notice` `the event has happened` `the day the event happened`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences`
            specified
            `the day on which it is made`
            `it is a rule or by-law`
            `it is published or to be published on the legislation website`
            (IF `it has been notified in the Gazette` THEN JUST `the day on which it was notified in the Gazette` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 63B(3), (4). Subordinate legislation must not be specified to commence or take effect on a day before the day it is made, unless the Act under which it is made expressly allows it; a provision made against this is of no effect.
@export Is a provision of a regulation, rule or by-law of no effect because it starts before the day it was made (s 63B(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day it says it starts` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the provision say it commences or takes effect?
      `the day on which it is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it made?
      `the Act expressly allows an earlier start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act under which it is made expressly provide for commencement or effect on a day before it is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a provision starting before the day it was made of no effect` IS
    `s 63B(3), (4): the provision of subordinate legislation is of no effect` `the day it says it starts` `the day on which it is made` `the Act expressly allows an earlier start`

§ `When a document is taken to be served (section 25)`

-- Used by the service questions: the way of serving, from a typed choice.
-- s 25(2) to (4). By prepaid post: when it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post; by fax: when it was sent to a current fax number, subject to evidence to the contrary;
-- by leaving it at the address: when it was left with the person; by giving it to a person: subsections (2) to (4) do not say, so the answer is not covered.
@export On which day is a document I serve, or am served with, taken to be served (s 25(2), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `the way it is served` IS A STRING @desc How is the document served? Type one of: by prepaid post; by fax; by leaving it at the address; by giving it to a person.
      `the day it was given, sent or left` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it given, sent or left?
      `its delivery day in the ordinary course of post is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was posted, is the day on which it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post known?
      `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc What is that day? (Answer with any date if it is not known.)
      `it was sent to a current fax number of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was sent by fax, was it sent to a current fax number of the recipient?
      `there is evidence to the contrary of the day of service by fax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that the fax was served on a different day?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is a document taken to be served` IS
    IF   `the way it is served` EQUALS "by prepaid post"
    THEN `Seat: the day of service` `by sending it by prepaid post` `my inputs`
    ELSE IF   `the way it is served` EQUALS "by fax"
         THEN `Seat: the day of service` `by sending it by fax` `my inputs`
         ELSE IF   `the way it is served` EQUALS "by leaving it at the address"
              THEN `Seat: the day of service` `by leaving it at the recipient's address with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and to live or be employed there` `my inputs`
              ELSE IF   `the way it is served` EQUALS "by giving it to a person"
                   THEN `Seat: the day of service` `by giving it to the recipient, an executive officer of the body or a person authorised to receive it` `my inputs`
                   ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `my inputs` MEANS
            `Service inputs` WITH
                `the day it was given, sent or left` IS `the day it was given, sent or left`
                `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post, if known` IS (IF `its delivery day in the ordinary course of post is known` THEN JUST `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post` ELSE NOTHING)
                `it was sent to a current fax number of the recipient` IS `it was sent to a current fax number of the recipient`
                `there is evidence to the contrary of the day of service by fax` IS `there is evidence to the contrary of the day of service by fax`

DECLARE `Service inputs` HAS
    `the day it was given, sent or left`                                               IS A DATE
    `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post, if known`    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `it was sent to a current fax number of the recipient`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is evidence to the contrary of the day of service by fax`                   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN method IS A `Method of serving a document`
      inputs IS A `Service inputs`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Seat: the day of service` MEANS
    `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served`
        method
        (inputs's `the day it was given, sent or left`)
        (inputs's `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post, if known`)
        (inputs's `it was sent to a current fax number of the recipient`)
        (inputs's `there is evidence to the contrary of the day of service by fax`)

-- s 25(1). A person may serve a document on an individual or a body by giving it to the recipient (an individual), an executive officer (a body) or a person the recipient authorises,
-- by prepaid post, by fax, or by leaving it at the recipient's address with someone who appears to be at least 16 and to live or be employed there.
@export May I serve my document in this way (s 25(1))?
GIVEN `I am serving a body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you are serving a company or other body, rather than an individual?
      `the way I serve it` IS A STRING @desc How do you serve it? Type one of: by giving it to someone; by prepaid post; by fax; by leaving it at the address.
      `the person I give it to` IS A STRING @desc If you give it to someone, who? Type one of: the recipient; an executive officer of the body; a person authorised by the recipient; someone else. (Type none if you do not give it to someone.)
      `they appear to be at least 16 years old` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you leave it at the address, does the person you leave it with appear to be at least 16 years old?
      `they appear to live or be employed there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person appear to live or be employed there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve my document in this way` IS
    IF   `the way I serve it` EQUALS "by prepaid post"
    THEN `s 25(1): a person may serve the document on the recipient in that way` `the kind of recipient` `sending it by prepaid post addressed to the recipient at the recipient's address`
    ELSE IF   `the way I serve it` EQUALS "by fax"
         THEN `s 25(1): a person may serve the document on the recipient in that way` `the kind of recipient` `sending it to the recipient by fax`
         ELSE IF   `the way I serve it` EQUALS "by leaving it at the address"
              THEN `s 25(1): a person may serve the document on the recipient in that way` `the kind of recipient`
                       (`leaving it, addressed to the recipient, at the recipient's address with someone` `they appear to be at least 16 years old` `they appear to live or be employed there`)
              ELSE IF   `the way I serve it` EQUALS "by giving it to someone"
                   THEN `s 25(1): a person may serve the document on the recipient in that way` `the kind of recipient` (`giving it to a person` `whom I give it to`)
                   ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the kind of recipient` MEANS IF `I am serving a body` THEN `a body` ELSE `an individual`
        `whom I give it to` MEANS
            IF   `the person I give it to` EQUALS "the recipient"
            THEN `the recipient`
            ELSE IF   `the person I give it to` EQUALS "an executive officer of the body"
                 THEN `an executive officer of the body`
                 ELSE IF   `the person I give it to` EQUALS "a person authorised by the recipient"
                      THEN `a person authorised by the recipient to receive the document`
                      ELSE `someone else`

§ `Sitting days of the Legislative Assembly (sections 63, 63C and 64)`

-- The sections below count sitting days, the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets.
-- The calendar of those days is a list of dates, given here as a list.
-- s 63(b). A regulation must be tabled within 6 sitting days after it is made.
@export By which day must a regulation be tabled in the Legislative Assembly (s 63(b))?
GIVEN `the day on which the regulation is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the regulation made?
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days does the Legislative Assembly meet? (Give the dates of its sitting days from the day the regulation is made onward.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must a regulation be tabled` IS
    `s 63(b): the last day on which the regulation must be tabled` `the day on which the regulation is made` `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`

-- s 63A(2)(b). A rule or by-law must be tabled within 6 sitting days after it is notified in the Gazette.
@export By which day must a rule or by-law be tabled in the Legislative Assembly (s 63A(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the day on which the rule or by-law is notified in the Gazette` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the rule or by-law notified in the Gazette?
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days does the Legislative Assembly meet? (Give the dates of its sitting days from the day of the notification onward.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must a rule or by-law be tabled` IS
    `s 63A(2)(b): the last day on which the rule or by-law must be tabled` `the day on which the rule or by-law is notified in the Gazette` `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`

-- s 63C(3). Notice of a resolution disallowing subordinate legislation must be given within 12 sitting days after it is tabled, or, if it was not tabled as required, 12 sitting days after the last sitting day on which it was required to be tabled.
@export By which day must notice of a resolution to disallow subordinate legislation be given (s 63C(3))?
GIVEN `it was tabled as section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the subordinate legislation tabled in accordance with section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b)?
      `the day on which it was tabled` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it tabled? (Answer with any date if it was not.)
      `the last sitting day on which it was required to be tabled` IS A DATE @desc What was the last sitting day on which it was required to be tabled?
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days does the Legislative Assembly meet? (Give the dates of its sitting days from the day it was tabled, or was required to be tabled, onward.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must notice of a resolution to disallow subordinate legislation be given` IS
    `s 63C(3): the last day on which notice of the resolution must be given`
        `it was tabled as section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b) requires` `the day on which it was tabled` `the last sitting day on which it was required to be tabled` `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`

-- s 64(2). Subordinate legislation the same in substance as disallowed legislation must not be made within 6 months after the disallowance unless the Assembly rescinds the resolution.
@export May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day (s 64(2))?
GIVEN `the day of the disallowance` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the earlier subordinate legislation disallowed?
      `the day on which the new subordinate legislation is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the new subordinate legislation made?
      `it is the same in substance or has the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new subordinate legislation the same in substance as the disallowed legislation, or does it have the same effect?
      `the Assembly has rescinded the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Legislative Assembly rescinded the resolution for disallowance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day` IS
    `s 64(2): the subordinate legislation may be made on the day` `the day of the disallowance` `the day on which the new subordinate legislation is made` `it is the same in substance or has the same effect` `the Assembly has rescinded the resolution`

§ `If a law I relied on has been repealed or has expired (sections 11 to 16)`

-- Situation: an Act or part of an Act has been repealed or has expired. Ask "Has this happened to you?" before showing the group.
-- s 12(c). The repeal of an Act does not affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it.
@export Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired or incurred under it (s 12(c))?
GIVEN `the right, privilege, obligation or liability was acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act or part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire the right, or incur the liability, under the Act or part that has been repealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired or incurred under it` IS
    IF   `the right, privilege, obligation or liability was acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act or part`
    THEN `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act or part`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 12(d). The repeal does not affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence against the repealed Act or part.
@export Does the repeal of an Act wipe out a penalty I incurred under it (s 12(d))?
GIVEN `the penalty, forfeiture or punishment was incurred in respect of an offence against the repealed Act or part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence against the Act or part that has been repealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the repeal of an Act wipe out a penalty I incurred under it` IS
    IF   `the penalty, forfeiture or punishment was incurred in respect of an offence against the repealed Act or part`
    THEN `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence against the repealed Act or part`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 12, closing words. An investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right or liability may be instituted, continued or enforced as if the repealing Act had not been made.
@export May a proceeding about a right or liability under a repealed Act still be started or continued (s 12)?
GIVEN `the proceeding is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act or part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy about a right or liability you acquired or incurred under the Act or part that was repealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a proceeding about a right or liability under a repealed Act still be started or continued` IS
    IF   `the proceeding is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act or part`
    THEN `s 12: the thing may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been made` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 14. Where an Act repeals a former Act and substitutes provisions, the repealed provisions continue in force until the substituted provisions commence.
@export Do the repealed provisions still apply on this day (s 14)?
GIVEN `the Act repeals a former Act in whole or in part and substitutes provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the new Act repeal the former Act (in whole or part) and put other provisions in its place?
      `the day on which the substituted provisions commence` IS A DATE @desc On what day do the substituted provisions commence?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the repealed provisions still apply on this day` IS
    `s 14: the repealed provisions continue in force on` `the Act repeals a former Act in whole or in part and substitutes provisions` `the day on which the substituted provisions commence` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 15. A reference to a provision that has been repealed and re-enacted is taken to be a reference to the re-enacted provision.
@export Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it (s 15)?
GIVEN `the law that repealed it is` IS A STRING @desc What kind of law repealed and re-enacted the provision? Type one of: an Act; a Commonwealth Act or legislative instrument; a State, Territory or New Zealand Act or subordinate legislation.
      `the law repeals and re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that law repeal and re-enact the provision, with or without changes?
      `the reference is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference you are asking about in an Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` IS
    IF   `the law that repealed it is` EQUALS "an Act"
    THEN `s 15: a reference to the provision repealed is taken to be a reference to the provision re-enacted` `an Act` `the law repeals and re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` `the reference is in an Act`
    ELSE IF   `the law that repealed it is` EQUALS "a Commonwealth Act or legislative instrument"
         THEN `s 15: a reference to the provision repealed is taken to be a reference to the provision re-enacted` `a Commonwealth Act or legislative instrument` `the law repeals and re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` `the reference is in an Act`
         ELSE IF   `the law that repealed it is` EQUALS "a State, Territory or New Zealand Act or subordinate legislation"
              THEN `s 15: a reference to the provision repealed is taken to be a reference to the provision re-enacted` `a State, Territory or New Zealand Act or subordinate legislation` `the law repeals and re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` `the reference is in an Act`
              ELSE NOTHING

§ `Fines and penalties (sections 38DC, 38F and 38G)`

-- s 38DC(3). Where an Act authorises a maximum fine to be set by subordinate legislation and does not give a different maximum for a body corporate, the maximum for a body corporate is 5 times that for an individual.
@export What is the most a company may be fined under subordinate legislation (s 38DC)?
GIVEN `the Act authorises a maximum fine for an offence under subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act authorise a maximum fine, to be imposed under subordinate legislation, for the offence?
      `the Act expressly authorises a different maximum for a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself say the maximum fine for a company or other body corporate is different from the maximum for an individual?
      `the most an individual may be fined, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most an individual may be fined, in penalty units?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most a company may be fined under subordinate legislation` IS
    `s 38DC(3): the maximum fine for a body corporate that may be imposed under the subordinate legislation`
        (`s 38DC(1): section 38DC applies to the provision` `the Act authorises a maximum fine for an offence under subordinate legislation` `the Act expressly authorises a different maximum for a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        `the most an individual may be fined, in penalty units`

-- s 38F(2). The fine that subordinate legislation prescribes must not exceed 100 penalty units, subject to the Act under which it is made.
@export Is the fine in this subordinate legislation within the limit of 100 penalty units (s 38F)?
GIVEN `the fine prescribed, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc What fine does the subordinate legislation prescribe, in penalty units?
      `the Act under which the legislation is made provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act under which the subordinate legislation is made provide a different limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the fine in this subordinate legislation within the limit` IS
    `s 38F(2): the fine prescribed is within the limit` `the fine prescribed, in penalty units` `the Act under which the legislation is made provides otherwise`

-- s 38G. A civil penalty indicates that the contravention may result in a penalty not exceeding the penalty specified in, or prescribed for, the provision.
@export Is the civil penalty I am asked to pay within what the provision allows (s 38G)?
GIVEN `the civil penalty specified or prescribed, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc What civil penalty does the provision specify or prescribe, in penalty units?
      `the civil penalty imposed or required to be paid, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc What civil penalty are you asked to pay, in penalty units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the civil penalty I am asked to pay within what the provision allows` IS
    `s 38G: the civil penalty is within the penalty specified or prescribed` `the civil penalty specified or prescribed, in penalty units` `the civil penalty imposed or required to be paid, in penalty units`

§ `Forms, appeals, money due and reprints (sections 65B, 68, 69 and 72B)`

-- s 68. Strict compliance with a form prescribed by or under an Act is not necessary; substantial compliance, or such compliance as the circumstances of the case allow, is sufficient.
@export Is my compliance with a prescribed form good enough (s 68)?
GIVEN `the form is prescribed by or under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form one prescribed by or under an Act?
      `my compliance is substantial, or as much as my circumstances allow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with the form substantially, or as far as your circumstances allow?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my compliance with a prescribed form good enough` IS
    `s 68: the compliance with the form is sufficient` `the form is prescribed by or under an Act` `my compliance is substantial, or as much as my circumstances allow`

-- s 65B(1). Subordinate legislation may provide for the review of, or a right of appeal against, a decision made under the legislation or the Act under which it is made or in force.
@export Can subordinate legislation give me a right of appeal or review (s 65B)?
GIVEN `the decision is made under the subordinate legislation or the Act under which it is made or in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one made under the subordinate legislation, or under the Act under which it is made or in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can subordinate legislation give me a right of appeal or review` IS
    `s 65B(1): the subordinate legislation may provide for review of, or a right of appeal against, the decision` `the decision is made under the subordinate legislation or the Act under which it is made or in force`

-- s 69. If money is due under an Act, it is recoverable in a court or tribunal having, in the Territory, civil jurisdiction to the extent of the amount due.
@export Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal (s 69)?
GIVEN `money is due under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money due under an Act?
      `the amount due` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is due, in dollars?
      `the court or tribunal has a monetary limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court or tribunal have a limit on the amount of money it can deal with in its civil jurisdiction?
      `the monetary limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that limit, in dollars? (Answer 0 if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal` IS
    `s 69: the money is recoverable in the court or tribunal`
        `money is due under an Act`
        `the amount due`
        (IF `the court or tribunal has a monetary limit` THEN JUST `the monetary limit` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 72B. A reprint shows the legislation as in force at the date stated in the reprint; an amendment that commences after that date is not included, unless it is identified as uncommenced.
@export Does the reprint I am reading include this amendment (s 72B)?
GIVEN `the day on which the amendment commences` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the amendment commence?
      `the date stated in the reprint` IS A DATE @desc What date does the reprint say it shows the legislation as at?
      `the reprint identifies the amendment as uncommenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the reprint mark the amendment as not yet commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the reprint I am reading include this amendment` IS
    `s 72B(2), (3): the reprint may include the amendment` `the day on which the amendment commences` `the date stated in the reprint` `the reprint identifies the amendment as uncommenced`
